# Git commit messages (qoomon conventional commits)
# https://gist.github.com/qoomon/5dfcdf8eec66a051ecd85625518cfd13

When generating a Git commit message for this repository, output **exactly one line** — the subject only.

## Required output shape

<type>(<optional scope>): <description>

Nothing else: no blank line, no body, no bullet lists, no file list, no footer.

- Types: feat, fix, refactor, perf, style, test, docs, build, ops, chore
- Scopes (examples): nav, catalog, i18n, breadcrumbs, config, seo, parser
- Description: imperative present tense; lowercase first letter; no trailing period
- Type must be spelled in full (e.g. `feat`, never truncated)
- Summarize the whole change in one line; do not enumerate each file or test

## Pick type (first match)

fix → feat → test → style → docs → build → ops → chore → perf → refactor

## Examples (entire commit message = one line)

feat(nav): add redirects for AI SDLC topics and improve breadcrumbs
fix(breadcrumbs): hide cluster title when flatNav is set
